hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"82","It is narrated from Usama bin Zaid that Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm informed him that during his caliphate, Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) wrote to him, asking him to write in detail about the charity of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), its rightful recipients, and also to write the hadith which you narrated to me from Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) regarding Umrah. Usama said: I asked Abu Bakr, ""Which hadith is narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)?"" Abu Bakr said: ""Umrah bint Abdul Rahman narrated the hadith to me; she heard Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) say, when people introduced new ways in the payment of charity: 'Glory be to Allah! This act resembles something found in the Book of Allah, the Exalted, in His statement: ""And they said, 'What is in the bellies of these cattle is exclusively for our men and forbidden to our women, but if it is born dead, then all of them are partners in it'"" [الانعام: 139] .'"""
